<title>FRANCE: FORECAST - Bank of France seen holding rates - poll.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Bank of France seen holding rates - poll.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of France is expected to hold its intervention rate unchanged at 3.15 percent after its monetary policy council meeting on Thursday.</p>
<p>The following gives a breakdown of forecasts by 15 economists polled by Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Ten out of 15 economists said they expected unchanged rates.</p>
<p>Bank/Financial Institution  Expect rate cut  Size of rate cut</p>
<p>    ABN Amro Finance			Yes	5 basis points</p>
<p>    Banque Paribas			  No</p>
<p>    Banques Populaires		    Yes	5 bp</p>
<p>    BFCE					No</p>
<p>    CCF					 No</p>
<p>    Caisse des Depots		     No</p>
<p>    Credit Lyonnais			 No</p>
<p>    CS First Boston			 No</p>
<p>    Deutsche Bank Paris		   No</p>
<p>    JP Morgan				 Yes	5 bp</p>
<p>    Louis Dreyfus Finance		 No</p>
<p>    Merrill Lynch			   Yes     10 bp</p>
<p>    Morgan Stanley			  No</p>
<p>    Nomura International		  No</p>
<p>    Sogeposte				 Yes     10 bp</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
